# VM basics (legacy `test/vm/01_basics`)

Same source files as the legacy corpus, referenced in place. The first three
cases carry dual checks (`avm/run` + `a2r/emit`); the a2r oracles are NEW,
independently reviewed snapshots under `oracle/` (see legacy-map.tsv).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/1"
  id: "lang.basic.hello"
  tags: ["pilot", "vm", "a2r"]
  source: { file: "vm/01_basics/001_hello/hello.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "vm", adapter: "avm", action: "run",
      expect: { completion: "success", stdout: { text: "hello\n", compare: "bytes" } } },
    { id: "rust", adapter: "a2r", action: "emit", tier: "trans-snapshot",
      options: { module_name: "hello" },
      expect: { completion: "success", artifacts: [
        { path: "hello.rs", file: "cases/pilot/oracle/lang.basic.hello.rs", compare: "bytes" } ] } }
  ]
}
```

